# The path this page used to live at. A visitor who bookmarked it, and a
# crawler that indexed it, both still ask for it; this keeps them working
# without a function and without an isolate.
#
# 301, not the 302 a two-field rule would default to: the move is permanent,
# so a browser may stop asking. Whatever the visitor arrived with after the
# ? rides along to the target, which is what keeps a campaign link's tracking
# intact across a move.
/old-home    /index.html    301
